    "message": "feat(bmad): module migrations, with the method module's v6 to v7 migration (#2935)\n\n* feat(bmad): module migrations, with the method module's v6 to v7 migration\n\nA module ships a migration as a TOML file beside its bmod.toml with a\n[migration] table. knowledge.py lists them; bmad migrate finds the one\nwhose detect signals match, follows its guide, and verifies its checklist.\n\nbmod-method/v6-v7-migration.toml carries the rules for moving a v6\nproject's artifacts into the v7 initiative layout: planning documents,\nepics.md and sprint-status.yaml into a ticket tree, inbox for loose work,\nand the store's repository and workspace choices asked as questions.\n\n* fix(bmad): migration listing checks every required key; v6 to v7 rules agree with tickets.py\n\nReview fixes. A migration is listed only when its [migration] table names\nthe record's module and carries every key migrate.md requires. A bad file\nis a migration problem, not a document one, and roster.toml is skipped.\nThe v6 to v7 file: a backlog epic gets no status line, remnants go to\ninbox by default, the plan is written before the backup and moved into\nthe initiative, the archive of done epics' story files is the one\nremoval and happens after commit, and the workspace move of _bmad is\ncarved out of the never-touch rule.\n\n* fix(bmad): address review on the v6 to v7 migration\n\nChecklist exempts the migration's own two versioned folders. A whole-epic\ndependency is written to the dependent epic file's after as well as the\ninitiative breakdown, which is where tickets.py gates it. A backlog story\nthat still has a file maps to draft. The bare-plus-worktree conversion\nbuilds beside the checkout, on the project's own base branch, and removes\nthe old checkout only after the new layout is verified. Naming a module\nnarrows migrate's candidates instead of skipping detect. knowledge.py\nrejects whitespace-only fields. Help rows match the questions flow."
  },
